{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The evidence supports a follow-up, but doesn’t establish the cause: the native item-width-8/action-width-16 model scored 0.65135 click AUC, while earlier compact models differed in context width and representation layout too.\n\nI’ll prepare a 2×2 comparison of item and action widths at 8 and 16, keeping context width at 16. This will test whether narrowing action width helps the compact model. The full-width and item-only controls will also check consistency with prior runs."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nprotocol='1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216'\nfixed=['full frozen train/validation populations and sample identities','100 released history positions, target action excluded, official_offline visibility','context width16; inherited 10 temporal blocks with uniform/nonaux/aux summaries (30 slots)','DIN unnormalized action-aware scorer64/32, four towers128/64 and Dice','auxiliary scorer/item gradients blocked, auxiliary context gradients allowed','host seed20262027, one epoch, batch8192, optimizers, BF16 and scoring']\nstudy={\n'id':'g1-r0014-item-action-capacity-factorial',\n'protocol_ref':protocol,\n'evidence_refs':['g2-r0004-context_only','baseline-din','g1-r0006-embedding_half','g1-r0006-dense_half','g1-r0010-copy8_interact16','g1-r0011-context16_item8','g1-r0012-native_context16_item12','g1-r0013-id8_attr16','g1-r0013-id16_attr8','g1-r0013-id8_attr8','g1-r0013-id16_attr16'],\n'question':'Does jointly narrowing historical action and item representations recover the unusually poor native item8/action16 result while reducing parameters and measured inference cost relative to the source, with supplied context held at16?',\n'hypothesis':'Observation: g1-r0013-id8_attr8 (all six item fields8, action/context16) scored click AUC0.651350616 versus0.660646940 for g1-r0013-id16_attr16. Individual ID/attribute reductions scored0.658232857/0.659659304. This nonlinear joint loss is unresolved. Earlier uniform-width8 and copy-expanded8 trials scored0.657781850 and0.659116842, but also changed context and/or layout, so they cannot identify an action effect. Provisional mechanism: the relative action/item capacity presented to the shared activation and readouts can interact with compact item representations; jointly narrowing action may improve quality beyond an additive action effect while retaining compact item storage. This is a test of a width interaction, not proof of semantic action dominance or a new architecture. Initializations, optimizer trajectories, Dice state and dense fan-in are live alternatives. AUC retention and actual cost improvement are separate requirements.',\n'nearest_work':[\n{'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived primary text lines219-274 inspected: field-concatenated embeddings, target-conditioned activation and unnormalized pooling are inherited. DIN does not establish this offline four-task action/item width interaction. No priority claim is made.'},\n{'source_ref':'framework:unirank/pytorch/layers/embeddings/feature_embedding.py','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned upstream ordered share_embedding and per-field embedding_dim handling inspected at lines55-117 and174-199. Use candidate-local metadata for native widths, preserve aliases; do not change host FeatureMap.'},\n{'source_ref':'trial://g1-r0013-id8_attr8','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Read standalone authorized ancestor. Replace its ID/attribute width factors with uniform item width and independent action width. Context stays16. All representation, compression, scorer functional-call, pooling and forward methods are inherited verbatim.'}],\n'inherited_components':['Released categorical input fields and masks; tied target/history lookup','Native per-field embedding widths with candidate-local metadata copy and ordered alias protection','30-slot uniform/feedback-stratified temporal compression','Action-aware unnormalized DIN scorer with Dice; four task towers','Auxiliary scorer and item stop-gradients; context auxiliary gradients; cloned auxiliary Dice buffers'],\n'proposed_difference':'A complete 2x2 factorial over uniform item width{8,16} and historical action width{8,16}, with context16 in every cell. Narrow action in lookup, scorer input and pooled readout together. No projections, duplicated coordinates, new loss, new labels or new input information. The item8/action16 and full16 cells are exact-width construction controls for prior committed endpoints. This is an empirical capacity-allocation follow-up, with architectural novelty unverified and not claimed.',\n'predictions':[\n'Let A(i,a) denote full-population click AUC for item width i/action width a. The predeclared interaction is D=[A(8,8)-A(8,16)]-[A(16,8)-A(16,16)]. D>0 and A(8,8)>A(8,16) would be preliminary directional evidence that action narrowing is more helpful with compact items; one seed is insufficient mechanism confirmation.',\n'The two action16 controls should reproduce prior point metrics: A(8,16)=0.651350616000785 and A(16,16)=0.660646940486458. Same-seed replay validates construction, not independent replication. Investigate a discrepancy before interpreting the factorial.',\n'Predeclared practical efficiency screen: compact AUC>=contemporaneous full16 AUC-0.0005; >=25% fewer total parameters; and >=5% lower model-only median batch latency, with p95 and end-to-end inference seconds also reported. These margins are operational screens, not significance/equivalence tests. Retention without uncertainty remains provisional.',\n'Native item8 cells should have about19.86M parameters versus32.06M full16, conditional on released alias/vocabulary layout. Action-only narrowing has very small sparse savings and is an attribution control rather than a useful storage intervention.',\n'Report all four task AUC/logloss, auxiliary mean separately, train/allocation/wall cost, peak memory, throughput and latency; compare inherited baseline and unchanged source. Use existing history bins and counts/positive/negative counts, emphasizing whether the long-history loss of the narrow-item control recovers. Slice analysis is exploratory.'],\n'falsifiers':[\n'D<=0 or A(8,8)<=A(8,16) fails the predicted direction for this implementation; it does not establish universal absence of action/item interaction.',\n'If the compact cell fails the AUC retention margin or the parameter/latency screens, this round does not demonstrate the proposed practical efficiency benefit even if D>0.',\n'If action narrowing helps both item widths equally, only an action main effect is supported; if repeats reverse D, the interaction remains unsupported.',\n'Endpoint reconstruction, alias, masking, causality, finite probability/loss or gradient gates failing blocks scientific interpretation; retain and charge failed attempts.'],\n'alternative_explanations':[\n'Width changes consume a different RNG stream and alter dense fan-in; deterministic replay is not a second seed and cannot distinguish rank/capacity from initialization.',\n'Dice/BatchNorm state and unnormalized pooled magnitude, optimizer conditioning and one-pass convergence could explain width interactions rather than relative semantic action information.',\n'The old compact versus new native comparison changes context and representation layout, and is motivation only; no cross-trajectory causal estimate is taken from it.',\n'ID/attribute width findings were not parameter matched. This factorial also changes sparse rank and dense input size together. Positive D does not identify which internal path mediates it.',\n'GPU alignment, loading variance and clock noise can make fewer parameters fail to reduce measured inference cost. End-to-end and model-only timings must remain distinct.',\n'Latest knowledge-usage declares Zenith-inspired ID/attribute separation but that prior executed factorial did not establish robust retention; EST was only considered. Neither supplies local action-width evidence or mandates this experiment.'],\n'contrasts':[\n{'parent_ref':'g1-r0013-id8_attr8','intervention':'item8_action8: narrow only historical action16->8 relative to item8_action16_control','control':'item8_action16_control, prior g1-r0013-id8_attr8; compare action contrast also at item16','held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':['action table rank, pooled value/scorer input width and dense fan-in move together','shape-dependent initialization and one-pass optimization','single seed; no mechanistic rescaling or capacity-matched replacement yet'], 'decision_if_supported':'Use the full factorial interaction to decide whether recovery is specific to compact items. If retention and measured cost screens pass, reserve paired repetitions and action scale/layout replacement before a strong claim.','decision_if_not_supported':'Retain the negative result; do not label previous item-width loss action-induced. Reconsider item rank or optimization only through a separately recorded discriminating study.'},\n{'parent_ref':'g2-r0004-context_only','intervention':'item16_action8: action-only narrowing with source item/context widths','control':'item16_action16_control and prior g1-r0013-id16_attr16; item8_action8 versus item8_action16_control completes the 2x2','held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':['same action changes as compact contrast','difference-in-differences is architecture/initialization interaction, not uniquely semantic action balance','no parameter-matched mechanism replacement in this first diagnostic'], 'decision_if_supported':'If the action-only effect explains the compact effect, report a main effect rather than interaction; judge practical efficiency separately.','decision_if_not_supported':'If action-only narrowing hurts while compact recovery occurs, prioritize paired repetition and a capacity-preserving action rescaling/layout control; do not infer mechanism from one seed.'},\n{'parent_ref':'g1-r0013-id16_attr16','intervention':'Reconstruct both action16 endpoints through the new independent-width helper','control':'g1-r0013-id16_attr16 full16 and g1-r0013-id8_attr8 item8/action16; original g2-r0004-context_only source','held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':['contemporaneous wall/inference timing varies','equal seed cannot establish robustness'], 'decision_if_supported':'Treat controls as compatibility and timing checks and interpret candidate contrasts against contemporaneous cells.','decision_if_not_supported':'Stop interpretation, audit construction/state/alias identities with host numerical checks, retain costs; no automatic unlogged retraining.'}],\n'cost_plan':{\n'estimate_ref':'g1-r0013-id8_attr8 wall287.323s and g1-r0013-id16_attr16 wall310.361s; frozen protocol estimated_unit_seconds481.348, trial_cap_seconds1203.369; runtime remaining146409.885s at resolution. Four cells estimate1200-1926s and <=4814s trial-cap sum, excluding ongoing preparation; actual host ledger is authoritative.',\n'all_variants_counted':True,\n'attribution_reserve':'Count all four cells including two endpoint replays, static preparation and host gates. Reserve at least8 additional estimated units (~3851s) for discriminating capacity-preserving action scale/layout replacements and paired repeats if consequential; these are future separate proposals, not authorization to train in this phase. At least three paired seeds should precede a repeated-support claim; new seeds require the authorized host interface and cannot be put into architecture config.',\n'assessment_reserve':'Reserve at least12 estimated units (~5777s) for frozen-suite paired final candidate/source/closest controls and closed assessment. Selection remains validation-only. Freeze source/config/checkpoint hashes, controls, seeds and commands before any withheld assessment; no holdout access here.',\n'stop_rule':'No training or installations in propose phase. Host must pass forward/backward/masking/finite-value/alias/parameter-count gates before full execution. Count failures, diagnostics, repeats and preparation. Never exceed resource ledger/deadline or1203.369s per-trial cap; stop if a useful complete comparison plus reserves no longer fits, endpoints disagree unresolved, integrity fails, or user stops. No test-driven iteration.'}\n}\nconfigs=[]\nfor name,i,a,role in [('item8_action8',8,8,'candidate'),('item16_action8',16,8,'control'),('item8_action16_control',8,16,'control'),('item16_action16_control',16,16,'control')]:\n cfg={'embedding_dim':16,'item_embedding_dim':i,'action_embedding_dim':a,'attention_hidden_units':[64,32],'tower_hidden_units':[128,64],'attention_normalization':'none','compression_routes':'uf','block_aux_scorer_grad':True,'block_aux_context_grad':False,'block_aux_item_grad':True}\n configs.append({'name':name,'file':'candidate.py' if role=='candidate' else name+'.py','role':role,'config':cfg,'note':f'Prospective item/action width cell{i}/{a}; context16. Standalone native-width module. Full action16 endpoints are construction/timing checks, not independent repeats. Static checks pending; host numerical/actual-cost gates required. No measured retention, speedup or novelty claim.'})\nproposal={'study':study,'parent_trial':'g2-r0004-context_only','variants':configs,'knowledge_assessments':[{'knowledge_id':'paper:din','decision':'used','rationale':'Read archived primary mechanism text through authorized source reader; target-conditioned unnormalized activation remains inherited, with no claim of exact original reproduction.','transformed_mechanism':'Independently vary item and historical-action native widths inside the existing four-task compressed adaptation; no new DIN mechanism claimed.','variant_names':[v['name'] for v in configs],'nearest_work_difference':'Prospective capacity-interaction diagnostic under frozen offline inputs, labels and recipe; prior work does not establish this effect.','falsifier':'The predicted positive interaction or practical retention/cost screens fail, or numerical gates fail.'}]}\nPath('/workspace/proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Recorded prospective study and four planned variants in proposal.json before candidate edits.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
